      "text_unit_id": "tu_0001",
      "verbatim_text": "1. In patients with ischemic heart disease and recurrent VA, with significant symptoms or ICD shocks despite optimal device programming and ongoing treatment with a beta blocker, amiodarone or sotalol is useful to suppress recurrent VA (S7.1.3-1–S7.1.3-3)."
